<title>UK: Mauritius November sugar output falls year/year.</title>
<headline>Mauritius November sugar output falls year/year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mauritius produced 47,565 tonnes of sugar in November 1996, down from the 67,827 tonnes turned out in the same month a year earlier, the Mauritius Sugar Syndicate said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sugar output in October 1996 amounted to 143,395 tonnes, the statement said.</p>
<p>The European Union accounted for the bulk of the country's November sugar exports, which totalled 37,182 tonnes compared with 36,780 tonnes in November 1995.</p>
<p>Cumulative sugar production for the first 11 months of last year amounted to 587,322 tonnes, up from the 526,027 tonnes in the same period in 1995. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
